          sanskrit: 'यत्र नेन्दीवरदलप्रख्यकान्तिर् अयं हरिः केनायं मानुषो जातो न च मानुषचेष्टितः तेनापि मर्त्यवासेन रतिर् अस्तीति विस्मयः',
          transliteration: 'yatra nendīvaradalaprakhyakāntir ayaṃ hariḥ kenāyaṃ mānuṣo jāto na ca mānuṣaceṣṭitaḥ tenāpi martyavāsena ratir astīti vismayaḥ',
          translation: 'Being thus addressed by Kaliya, Krishna said— "You must not wait here any more; go immediately, withyour family and followers, to the sea. Garuda, the enemy of the serpents, will not injure thee if he sees the impressions o( my feetupori your hoooj." Having said this, Hari liberated the serpent-king, who, respectfully bowing to his victor, went to the ocean accom- panied by all his wives, servants and children, leaving the sight of all and the pool he had lived in. When the snake had departed, the cow-herds received back Govinda as one risen from dead and embraced him and bathed his forehead with tears of joy. Others, considering the water of the river pure, were filled with surprise, and chanted the glory of Krishna, who is above the influence of actions. Being thus glorified by his illustrious exploits and eulogized by the cow-herda and their wives, Krislina came back to Traja.',
          hindi: 'गा: पालयन्तौ च पुन: सहितो बलकेशवौ। तत्तु तालवनं दिव्यं धेनुको नाम दानव:। हे राम है कृष्ण सदा थेनुकेनेष रक्ष्यते। इति गोपकुमाराणां श्रुत्वा संकर्षणो बच: ।',
