          hindi: 'केशी चापि बलोदग्र: कंसदूतप्रचोदित: । तस्य हेषितशब्देन गोपाला हैत्यवाजिन:। अलं त्रासेन गोपाला: केशिन: कि भयातुरैः । किमनेनाल्‍पसारेण हेषिताटोपकारिणा।',
          explanation: 'When they had finished, Krishna rftmaind silent for some time as if hurt and wounded and then said to them. Herds- men, if you are not ashamed of my relationship, if 1 have deserved your praise, then what necessity have you to discuss thus concerning me ? If you have any love for me, if I merit your praise, then consider me as your friend. I am nither a god, nor a Gandharba nor a Yaksha nor a demon— I am born as thy friend and you should not think otherwise of me." PARASAKA said :— Being addressed thus, O great Muni\' the cow-herds remained*silent and went iuto the woods',
