          transliteration: 'utsṛjya dvārakāṃ kṛṣṇas tyaktvā mānuṣyam ātmabhūḥ sāṃśo viṣṇumayaṃ sthānaṃ praviveśa punar nijam',
          translation: 'PARAsARAsaid : — At theholy place of Pindarika,Viswamitra, Kanwa and the great sage, Nárada, were seen by some boys of the Yadu family. Inflated with their youths and influenced by predestined results, tliey dressed and adorned Samba, the son of Jámbavati, as a female and taking her to the sages, they addressed them with usual reverence, saying : — " What child with this female, the wife of Bábru, who is anxious to have a son, give birth to ?" The sages, who were gifted with divine wisdom, enraged at this insult, said : — " She vvill give birth to a club that will exterminate the entire Yádava race."',
